Large lists of models (sandialabs/PEAT#20), such as relay configurations with thousands of registers, are no longer extremely slow to parse and export. Deduplication of model lists (:func:`~peat.data.data_utils.dedupe_model_list`) now indexes model values instead of comparing every model with every other model, which is roughly linear instead of quadratic. :func:`~peat.data.data_utils.merge_models` now actually removes duplicates when combining lists of models (previously the deduplicated result was discarded, so merged devices could accumulate duplicate items), and no longer duplicates modules that don't have a slot or serial number when merging devices. Lists with 5,000 or more items are now deduplicated by :meth:`~peat.data.models.DeviceData.purge_duplicates` instead of being skipped. Parsing no longer compares whole devices by value when checking if a device is in the datastore or part of the current parse, which converted every device to a dict on each comparison.
